1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,980
Here's a CRM I built for another lender,

2
00:00:03,220 --> 00:00:05,140
set up the way Excel Capital would use

3
00:00:04,940 --> 00:00:05,300
it.

4
00:00:05,387 --> 00:00:07,147
Every morning starts on Today.

5
00:00:07,527 --> 00:00:09,827
At the top: repayments that didn't come in,

6
00:00:09,987 --> 00:00:11,607
straight from your repayments app,

7
00:00:11,707 --> 00:00:12,407
with the reason.

8
00:00:12,732 --> 00:00:15,592
Click See repayments, and you get every collection:

9
00:00:15,972 --> 00:00:17,572
what came in, and what failed.

10
00:00:17,810 --> 00:00:21,910
Below that: follow-ups, new applications from your website

11
00:00:21,710 --> 00:00:24,570
and your brokers, and renewals that are ready.

12
00:00:24,706 --> 00:00:28,466
Click Deals. Every application moves left to right,

13
00:00:28,646 --> 00:00:29,886
from new to funded.

14
00:00:30,083 --> 00:00:31,743
When a broker sends one in,

15
00:00:31,663 --> 00:00:32,943
type the business name.

16
00:00:33,283 --> 00:00:34,963
If another broker sent it first,

17
00:00:35,263 --> 00:00:36,223
it tells you.

18
00:00:36,908 --> 00:00:38,088
Before a deal funds,

19
00:00:38,208 --> 00:00:39,368
click Send bank link.

20
00:00:39,548 --> 00:00:41,988
The business approves repayments in their own bank.

21
00:00:42,125 --> 00:00:44,485
When they do, the checklist ticks itself.

22
00:00:45,065 --> 00:00:46,065
Click Mark funded.

23
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:47,920
Repayments start on their own,

24
00:00:47,980 --> 00:00:49,920
and every one shows up on the deal.

25
00:00:50,137 --> 00:00:52,237
Once a business has paid back half,

26
00:00:52,517 --> 00:00:53,637
it's ready to renew.

27
00:00:54,937 --> 00:00:56,497
One place for every deal,

28
00:00:56,657 --> 00:00:59,057
from first enquiry to last repayment.
